# sshd for every container. The bot (php/service) logs in as root with
# its key to run commands; nothing else needs a shell or forwarding.
# the bot's public key, read on every login: php makes a new key on each
# start, and a copy taken at this container's start would go stale
AuthorizedKeysFile	/ssh/key.pub
# host keys: the ed25519 key stays the same across restarts (./sshhost,
# made by php) and the bot checks it on every login; the others are made
# at each container start (ssh-keygen -A) for other clients (DNSTT).
# RSA keys sign with rsa-sha2-256/512 only (OpenSSH's default), not with
# SHA-1 "ssh-rsa": the bot's RSA key works so with libssh2 1.11+.
HostKey /etc/ssh/pinned/ssh_host_ed25519_key
HostKey /etc/ssh/ssh_host_ecdsa_key
HostKey /etc/ssh/ssh_host_rsa_key
LogLevel QUIET

PermitRootLogin prohibit-password
PasswordAuthentication no
KbdInteractiveAuthentication no
PermitEmptyPasswords no
AllowTcpForwarding no
AllowAgentForwarding no
AllowStreamLocalForwarding no
X11Forwarding no
GatewayPorts no
PermitTunnel no
PermitUserRC no
PermitUserEnvironment no
Subsystem	sftp	internal-sftp

# DNSTT tunnel account (exists only in the dnstt container): password
# login for tunnelling (ssh -D / -L) only. No commands, shell or sftp:
# a session just stays open so clients that ask for one keep working.
# Which addresses the tunnel may reach is limited by iptables
# (scripts/start_dnstt.sh).
Match User vpnbot
	PasswordAuthentication yes
	AuthorizedKeysFile none
	AllowTcpForwarding local
	PermitOpen any
	ForceCommand /usr/bin/tail -f /dev/null
